## Objective Statement

### Formal Objective

The Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) shall provide adaptive vehicle intelligence by continuously perceiving, interpreting, reasoning about, and responding to its operating environment in order to support safe, effective, and context-appropriate vehicle operation.

---

### Objective Intent

Establish the primary functional capability of AVIA from which all subsequent functional objectives are derived.

---

### Success Criteria

This objective is considered satisfied when the system demonstrates the ability to:

- Perceive relevant information from its operating environment.
- Interpret the current operating context.
- Generate context-appropriate decisions.
- Support execution of approved actions.
- Adapt its behavior in response to changes in the operating environment while remaining within defined system constraints.

---

### Engineering Constraints

- The objective shall remain solution-independent.
- The objective shall not prescribe implementation technologies or algorithms.
- All derived functional objectives shall remain traceable to this objective.

---

### Assumptions

- AVIA operates within an environment where relevant operational information can be perceived.
- Supporting objectives will define the detailed capabilities required to realize this root objective.
